Task: # Task: construct and wire a batch execution module

Add `pkg.batch` with three real product files: `__init__.py`, `contracts.py`, and `runner.py`. Export `BatchResult` and `run_batch` from the package. Results must preserve input order and contain `index`, `item`, `ok`, `value`, and `error`. Each work function exception becomes a failed result; `stop_on_error=True` stops after recording the first failed item.

Wire the real batch runner through service, worker, and CLI. Resolve the stop-on-error default from config only when no explicit setting is given. Register the batch capability and serialize the same result fields. Keep existing single-item APIs working. A fresh Python process must be able to import the completed package.

Only edit these product paths: new `pkg/batch/__init__.py`, `contracts.py`, `runner.py`; existing `pkg/service.py`, `worker.py`, `cli.py`, `__init__.py`, `registry.py`, `serializers.py`, `config.py`. Protected tests are immutable. `pkg/legacy_batch.py` is an unrelated same-named context file. Keep execution local and deterministic.

